## 3. Data Governance

### 3.1 Data Classification and Retention

| Data Type | Sensitivity | Retention |
|---|---|---|
| Raw social media text | **Highest** | 0 days — never stored |
| Anonymised feature vectors | High | 30 days rolling |
| Risk scores | High | 90 days |
| Aggregated population data | Medium | 12 months |
| Audit logs | Low | 24 months |

### 3.2 Data Safety Recommendations

1. **Encryption at rest and in transit** — AES-256 minimum for stored feature vectors and risk scores
2. **Zero-knowledge architecture** — system administrators cannot access clinical data
3. **Minimal data collection** — collect only what is necessary for risk scoring
4. **Regular penetration testing** — quarterly security audits
5. **Breach response protocol** — 72-hour notification under GDPR; 3-day under PDPA
6. **Data residency** — no cross-border transfer of health data without explicit consent and legal basis

### 3.3 Data Minimisation Principles

- No names or identifiers stored with feature vectors
- No raw text retained after feature extraction
- Purpose limitation — screening only; cannot be used for academic assessment or discipline
- Pseudonymisation — internal IDs only
- Geographic restriction — data processed and stored within deployment country

