## 5. AI Bias and Equity

### 5.1 Three Types of AI Bias (Chee, 2026)

| Bias Type | Description | Pipeline Risk | Mitigation |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Representation Bias** | Training data over-represents certain populations | Weibo data over-represents mainland China | Singapore-specific validation in Phase 2 |
| **Cultural Bias** | Model encodes one cultural context as default | Mainland Chinese norms may differ from SG/HK/TW | Multi-country validation data |
| **Stereotype Bias** | Features encode harmful generalisations | Academic stress framing may penalise high achievers | Context-specific feature sensitivity audit |

### 5.2 Social Determinants of Health — Equity Considerations (Chee, 2026)

| SDOH Factor | Pipeline Risk | Mitigation |
|---|---|---|
| Socioeconomic status | Low-income adolescents less present on social media | Complement with school-based surveys |
| Digital access | Those without smartphones invisible to system | Multi-channel data collection |
| Education level | Low health literacy affects self-report quality | Plain language interface design |
| Language | Non-Mandarin/English speakers underserved | Expand language coverage in future versions |
| Geographic | Rural/isolated adolescents have different patterns | Context-specific model calibration |
| Ethnicity | Chinese-dominant training data | Stratified validation by ethnicity |

### 5.3 Cognitive Bias in Clinical Decision-Making (Chee, 2026)

| Bias | Description | Mitigation |
|---|---|---|
| **Availability heuristic** | Over-weighting memorable past cases | Training on base rates; show population context |
| **Confirmation bias** | Discounting high score when student seems "fine" | Interface shows trend data not just current score |
| **Anchoring** | First score anchors future expectations | Clear display of score trajectory and changes |

